    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.53), our two strongest plays. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Littell, who sports a 4.63 xERA, allowing **Jackson Merrill** to leverage a +13% dynamic platoon boost and a favorable park factor. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** thrives in his matchup against Painter; while Painter is a developing arm, the combination of a 4.32 xERA and beneficial wind conditions driving the ball out yields a high efficiency score. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.67) also warrants attention as a top-tier start, capitalizing on a significant +14% platoon edge against Canning to punch well above his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Josh Jung** (58.60) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.23). While **Josh Jung** ultimately secured the starting 3B spot, the marginal difference in their scores reflects the risk associated with facing Wacha. **Miguel Vargas** sits just outside the \"Strong\" start threshold; he remains a viable pivot, but the edge for **Josh Jung** was dictated by his batting order stability. We are also monitoring the stagnant nature of our bench, as **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Drake Baldwin** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our late-inning versatility. \n\nRisks are concentrated in the bottom third of our lineup. **Brayan Rocchio** (40.91) is on the precipice of our bench floor due to a suppressed order position (#9) and a tough southpaw matchup against Suarez. Additionally, **Liam Hicks** (41.56) faces McLean, whose 3.03 xERA is the most daunting we face today; we are betting on his order placement (#2) and wind assistance to provide just enough efficiency to justify the start over speculative depth pieces like **Jacob Wilson** or **Nasim Nunez**. While our core\u2014including **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Sam Antonacci**\u2014is well-positioned to drive volume in R/RBI, we remain vigilant for in-game defensive shifts that could impact our stolen base opportunities.",
